Subject: Cantor Composed Read-Only Semantic Inspection P0 Justification

@ [justification_uuid] cb04aa4c-1176-4761-b04d-f49d761891d6
@ [specification_uuid] 8e08875a-6877-4c07-9752-b96771fb0b33

& [Need]
  + the three published kernels are useful but still require every caller to invent orchestration correspondence and failure semantics
  + one governed composition makes Cantor usable as an auditable semantic inspection engine before any host process or adapter authority is opened

& [Choice]
  + compose existing public pure APIs rather than duplicate their algorithms or import live cantor_scribe Reader storage or server code
  + return compact assembly coordinates plus exact nested query and excerpt receipts rather than duplicate the full assembly in the result
  + fix P0 projection to every hit on one page so correspondence is exact and no selector language is invented

& [Tradeoff]
  + the request still carries the supplied project and therefore favors proof and portability over memory efficiency
  + the64-hit composition cap is stricter than the nested finder and intentionally bounds repeated excerpt work

& [Authority]
  + implementation authority is limited to CRSI-001 through CRSI-024 and CRSI-A01 through CRSI-A05
